WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.710
An essay page.

2
00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:06.220
At the top, a neat paragraph
of history: in 1834,

3
00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:07.780
a new Poor Law.

4
00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:11.630
A highlighter sweeps down the
page, and skips it completely.

5
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:15.770
Further down sits Scrooge, on
the poor who would rather die:

6
00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:19.520
"they had better do it, and
decrease the surplus population."

7
00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:21.340
The history is accurate.

8
00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:24.190
So when does knowing it actually count?

9
00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:27.920
In this mission, you'll learn
what context really means:

10
00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:30.940
the world a text was
written in, and read in.

11
00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:35.740
You'll uncover the facts behind
Stave 1: the Poor Law of 1834,

12
00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:39.600
its workhouses, and a
book published in 1843.

13
00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:44.720
And you'll sort students' sentences, and
decide which ones make the history count.

14
00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:48.530
Your mission: work out when
knowing that earns marks.
